{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && git check-ignore -v cores/bench/implementation_notes.md || true'","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\n- Replaced the signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned\n  multipliers in `rtl/alu.sv` with one unsigned 32-by-32 product. MUL uses\n  its low half and MULHU uses its high half. MULH subtracts `b` when `a` is\n  negative and `a` when `b` is negative; MULHSU subtracts `b` when `a` is\n  negative. Corrections are accumulated modulo 2^32 before subtracting from\n  the product's upper word.\n- No deviations from the proposed arithmetic or latency. ALTOPS stand-ins\n  are unchanged.\n- Concern: the local Gowin timing run printed one placement result at\n  45.091 MHz (18 logic levels); its critical paths still run from the\n  forwarding unit through EX/ALU to the memory-side outputs. This single\n  result does not establish an improvement against a same-run baseline.\n- Local checks: Verilator lint passed; `make test TARGET=bench` passed 5/5;\n  formal passed 53/53 checks with ALTOPS; `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`\n  passed both ELF runs. The default `make cosim` build initially used\n  `NRET=2`, which does not match this core's nret=1 port set; rerunning with\n  `NRET=1` succeeded.\n.gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\tcores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
