{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git diff --check && test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,100p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\n# Implementation notes — Predecode divider busy control\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added `ctrl_t.is_div` and a decoder output that asserts it only for the\n  validated OP encoding with `funct7=1` and `funct3[2]=1` (DIV, DIVU, REM,\n  REMU).\n- Captured the decoded bit in the existing ID/EX control register.\n- Changed EX divider detection to `in.valid && in.ctrl.is_div`. The ALU-op\n  comparisons used to choose signed versus unsigned operation and quotient\n  versus remainder remain in place; they do not feed `div_busy`.\n- Extended the decoder unit test to check `is_div` across all eight M-extension\n  arithmetic encodings.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nNo functional deviations from the hypothesis. `is_div` also resides in the\nshared control struct used by later pipeline bundles, where synthesis can\nremove it if unused. Timing option 0 still reports the fetch/hazard/ID feedback\nroute as the worst path; the timing run reported 45.184 MHz. One placement\noption is not enough to compare the evaluator's median Fmax against baseline.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass (`verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP ...`).\n- Formal: pass, 53 checks passed and 0 failed, using\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`.\n- Unit tests: pass, all 5 bench pytest tests passed, including decoder checks.\n- Cosim: pass, both selftest and CoreMark passed using\n  `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`, matching `core.yaml`'s `nret: 1`. The\n  initial default-NRET invocation did not compile because the harness defaulted\n  to 2 and referenced channel-1 ports absent from this single-retire core.\n- Gowin timing: option 0 reported 45.184 MHz; worst path crosses the\n  regfile/ID/EX/EX/IF/hazard/ID loop.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
