{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git diff -- cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv && test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ndiff --git a/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv b/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\nindex d758bfe..4111086 100644\n--- a/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+++ b/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n@@ -60,6 +60,14 @@ module ex_stage (\n     .out (alu_result)\n   );\n \n+  // Loads and stores use a dedicated effective-address path. It starts\n+  // from the forwarded rs1 value directly, bypassing the ALU operand\n+  // selectors and the ALU's operation-result mux.\n+  logic        mem_op;\n+  logic [31:0] effective_addr;\n+  assign mem_op        = in.ctrl.mem_read || in.ctrl.mem_write;\n+  assign effective_addr = rs1 + in.imm;\n+\n   // ── Iterative radix-2 divider ─────────────────────────────────────────\n   logic        div_op;\n   logic        div_is_signed;\n@@ -266,7 +274,9 @@ module ex_stage (\n       // For JAL/JALR, the rd_wdata is PC+4 (return address), not the ALU's\n       // sum (which is the jump target). The MEM/WB register's read-data\n       // mux only kicks in for LOADs, so we route PC+4 here.\n-      reg_q.alu_result    <= in.ctrl.is_jump ? (in.pc + 32'd4) : exec_result;\n+      reg_q.alu_result    <= in.ctrl.is_jump ? (in.pc + 32'd4)\n+                            : mem_op          ? effective_addr\n+                                              : exec_result;\n `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n       reg_q.write_data    <= rs2;\n       reg_q.rs1_val       <= rs1;\n# Implementation notes: direct effective address adder\n\n## Change\n\nAdded a dedicated `rs1 + immediate` adder in `rtl/ex_stage.sv`. Its `rs1`\ninput is the already-forwarded EX operand, and its sum is selected into the\nEX/MEM `alu_result` field for loads and stores. Jumps retain the PC+4 result,\nand other instructions retain the existing ALU/divider result. No pipeline\nstage or memory-operation cycle was added.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nThe implementation follows the proposed EX-stage-only change. The local\ntiming report still shows a critical path through the general ALU multiplier\nto the data-memory address logic; the new sum does not remove that path for\nnon-memory instructions. The measured local placement reported 44.206 MHz\nfor option 0, so improvement is not established by this run.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Verilator lint: passed.\n- Formal: passed, 53 checks and 0 failures. The first invocation lacked the\n  required `RTL_DIR` and `CORE_NAME` variables; rerun as\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` passed.\n- Cosim: passed for 2 ELF files with `NRET=1`. The default `make cosim`\n  build expects NRET=2 and fails to compile against this core's NRET=1 port\n  set; `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed.\n- Timing: `make timing TARGET=bench` completed. Option 0 reported 44.206 MHz;\n  the critical memory-address paths still pass through `u_alu/mul_ss`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
