ed locally — the unused\n@@ -32,7 +60,7 @@ module alu (\n     mul_su = $signed({{32{a[31]}}, a}) * $signed({32'b0, b});\n \n     case (op)\n-      ALU_ADD:    out = a + b;\n+      ALU_ADD:    out = add_result;\n       ALU_SUB:    out = a - b;\n       ALU_AND:    out = a & b;\n       ALU_OR:     out = a | b;\n# Implementation notes\n\n- Replaced `ALU_ADD`'s 32-bit `a + b` with a four-byte carry-select sum in\n  `rtl/alu.sv`. The low byte computes its sum and carry. Each upper byte\n  precomputes carry-in-zero and carry-in-one sums; the prior block's carry\n  selects the result. Other ALU operations and ALTOPS substitutions are\n  unchanged.\n- No pipeline state or latency changed.\n- Concerns: the local Gowin timing run reported 49.387 MHz (25.542 ns worst\n  path), with the longest reported path in the PC/control loop. Forwarding to\n  the data-memory address was also close at about 25.5 ns. This single timing\n  run does not demonstrate an Fmax improvement over the stored 50.463 MHz\n  figure; placement and timing should be compared by the evaluator's full\n  placement sweep.\n- Local lint: passed with the requested Verilator command.\n- Local formal: passed, 53 checks and 0 failures.\n- Local cosim: passed for selftest and CoreMark with `NRET=1`, matching\n  `cores/bench/core.yaml`. The default `make cosim` build uses `NRET=2` and\n  fails to compile its harness against this core's single-channel RVFI ports;\n  `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
