{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short && git diff --stat && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Change\n\nIn `ex_stage.sv`, compute `rs1 + imm` concurrently for the ID/EX, EX/MEM,\nand MEM/WB rs1 sources. The existing rs1 forwarding select chooses among\nthose completed sums. Loads and stores register that selected effective\naddress in the existing EX/MEM `alu_result` field; other instructions retain\nthe general ALU result. This leaves the pipeline latency and forwarding\ncontrols unchanged.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nThere were no behavioral deviations from the hypothesis. The EX/MEM\n`alu_result` field already feeds memory addresses, so no pipeline bundle or\nMEM-stage changes were needed. The extra candidate adders increase\ncombinational logic. `make timing TARGET=bench` reported 50.248 MHz for\nplace option 0; its critical path was ID control to the fetch PC at 25.196 ns,\nwith the forwarding-to-data-memory path at 25.195 ns. This run does not show a\nmaterial Fmax improvement, and the two paths are effectively tied.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`):\n  pass, 53 checks and 0 failures.\n- Cosim: the default `make cosim TARGET=bench` build selected NRET=2 and\n  failed to compile against this core's nret=1 port set. Rerunning as\n  `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed both tested ELF programs.\n- Timing: completed; result and paths are summarized above.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
