{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"Formal found one real corner case: a misaligned load’s write enable was still high while its address was in EX/MEM, so the captured selector could forward its data even though MEM later suppresses the write. I’m moving that alignment check into EX’s trap control as well, so the producer is marked non-writing before ID captures a selector. Then I’ll rerun formal."}}
