{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && sed -n '1,200p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- MEM now exposes its current final writeback value to ID, selecting the\n  aligned and extended load result for loads and the ALU result otherwise.\n- ID resolves an EX/MEM producer match and captures that value into ID/EX.\n  The ID/EX producer retains priority and uses a one-bit EX forwarding select;\n  EX no longer has a MEM/WB forwarding input or selection.\n- ID branch comparison continues to use EX/MEM and valid WB values. The\n  existing dmem stall holds ID/EX until load response data is ready, and the\n  register file retains its WB write-through behavior.\n- Also removed `ex_div_busy` from `flush_if`: `ex_div_busy` already holds\n  ID/EX, so masking the combinational IF/ID payload was redundant. This\n  removes a long control-to-branch feedback path without changing when the\n  PC or ID/EX advances.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint: passed with the requested command.\n- Formal: passed, 53 checks and 0 failures, using\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`.\n- Cosim: passed both ELF runs with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`, matching\n  this core's `nret: 1` contract. The default `make cosim TARGET=bench`\n  invocation uses NRET=2 and fails to compile because this core correctly\n  has no channel-1 ports.\n- Gowin timing: place option 0 reported 58.566 MHz. The worst path is now\n  the imem stall input through IF, RF, ID and back to the PC; the next paths\n  include immediate ID/EX forwarding through the ALU to dmem.\n\n## Concerns\n\nThe older EX/MEM load data path is combinational from dmem read data into\nID/EX, relying on the existing dmem-ready stall to prevent capture before\nthe response is valid. Formal and the randomized-stall cosim passed. The\nmeasured critical path has moved away from the older WB bypass, but the IF\nstall/branch feedback path remains a timing limit.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
