{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short && sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added EX/MEM fields for the low 16-bit address sum and carry, and the two\n  carry-select high-half sums.\n- EX computes those partial sums from the forwarded `rs1` and the immediate.\n  The existing EX/MEM register holds them during dmem stalls.\n- MEM assembles the address from the registered partials for `dmemAddr`,\n  access alignment checks, load lane selection, and RVFI aligned memory\n  metadata. Non-memory instructions continue to use `alu_result` for\n  writeback; `dmemAddr` is irrelevant while the memory enables are low.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- The partial sums are captured on every EX/MEM transfer, though MEM consumes\n  them only for loads and stores. This avoids adding a separate address-path\n  control mux in EX.\n- The added 49 EX/MEM bits increase register use. The Gowin timing target did\n  increase register count. `make timing TARGET=bench` first reported an\n  IF0008 resource-limit error for `dmem_3`, then completed on retry. Place\n  option 0 reported 52.389 MHz and 20 logic levels. The five listed worst\n  paths were decode/control to PC or forwarding through EX to the ALU result;\n  `dmemAddr` was not among them.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 checks, using the auto-detected `nret: 1` wrapper/config.\n- Cosim: pass, 2 ELF runs with `NRET=1` to match this core's channel-0-only\n  interface. The default `NRET=2` build does not match this core's existing\n  port set.\n- Gowin timing: place option 0 reported 52.389 MHz; an initial resource-limit\n  error did not recur on retry.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
