{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"The first FPGA sweep shows the new worst path is divider control feeding fetch stall, and the load-use interlock is conservative enough to hold a consumer until WB. I’m tightening that interlock: make the MEM-stage extended load value available to the operand capture mux, so consumers can advance as soon as the load reaches MEM. The data-memory stall still holds the capture boundary until the bus is ready."}}
