{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- `ex_stage` now exposes the combinational EX completion record as well as\n  its registered EX/MEM output.\n- `mem_stage` separates the held EX/MEM bus request from the record being\n  formatted for completion, and can promote a saved MEM/WB record.\n- `core` captures one eligible younger instruction into a `mem_wb_t` skid\n  register during a dmem stall. EX/MEM and its request remain held until the\n  handshake. The memory instruction enters MEM/WB on the handshake, then the\n  skid retires on the next cycle.\n- `hazard_unit` consumes the captured ID/EX instruction once, blocks further\n  issue while the skid is occupied, prevents redirects while the memory\n  operation is pending, and checks load dependencies at the release boundary.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- No `core_pkg.sv` changes were needed; the existing `mem_wb_t` carries the\n  skid record.\n- Admission is limited to valid non-memory ALU class instructions. Branches,\n  jumps, divides, and instructions whose encoded source fields match a\n  pending load destination remain held until the memory operation finishes.\n  The source check is conservative for immediate instructions and can skip\n  some otherwise safe overlaps.\n- Gowin timing reported 35.958 MHz for placement option 0, with the worst\n  path through EX address generation and the memory read-data path.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: 53 passed,\n  0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass; selftest and CoreMark both passed.\n  The unqualified `make cosim` defaults to `NRET=2`, which does not match this\n  core's declared `nret: 1`.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench`: pass; Fmax 35.958 MHz (placement option 0).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
