{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r10s1.yaml && cat cores/bench/worktrees/.agent.hyp-20260930-002-r9s1.last && rg -n 'r10s1|formal_failed|insn_beq_ch0|Pipeline the execute datapath' cores/bench\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-002-r10s1\ntitle: \"Pipeline the execute datapath\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The strongest measured timing path runs through EX operand forwarding and the ALU before reaching the memory address path. The existing stage performs wide operand selection, arithmetic, and result registration in one cycle, which is the main remaining structural timing bottleneck after moving conditional branch resolution into ID.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split EX into an operand stage and a result stage. The first stage resolves the existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypasses and registers the selected operands and instruction metadata; the second stage performs ALU and effective-address generation and registers the result for MEM. Use explicit stage-valid and backpressure control so a dmem stall holds both EX stages and older state without replaying or dropping an instruction; when a divide occupies the result stage, retain the younger operand-stage instruction and stop fetch/decode until it can advance. A redirect resolved in the result stage must squash the younger operand-stage and decode instructions, while ID-resolved conditional branches retain their current behavior. Separating bypass selection from the wide ALU work should shorten the critical cycle while maintaining one-instruction-per-cycle flow for independent instructions.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define the payload and valid state needed between the operand and result portions of EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture forwarded operands in the first EX stage and compute/register ALU, address, redirect, and divide results in the second stage with no instruction replay under backpressure.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the added EX-stage boundary and propagate stage-valid, stall, and redirect control through the pipeline.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Backpressure both EX stages for dmem waits and iterative divides, and flush younger state on result-stage redirects.\"\ncat: cores/bench/worktrees/.agent.hyp-20260930-002-r9s1.last: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
