{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 12 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && rg -n \"r11s1|Predecode EX forwarding|forward.*selector|forward_w_en|fwd_rs\" cores/bench/experiments cores/bench'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Split operand forwarding from execute\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current best's measured critical path starts at MEM/WB forwarding state and runs through the EX forwarding network and ALU toward the data-memory address output. These are two wide selection and arithmetic operations in one timing stage. A structural pipeline boundary between operand selection and execution can let each settle in its own cycle without lowering steady-state issue rate.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current best's measured critical path starts at MEM/WB forwarding state and runs through the EX forwarding network and ALU toward the data-memory address output. These are two wide selection and arithmetic operations in one timing stage. A structural pipeline boundary between operand selection and execution can let each settle in its own cycle without lowering steady-state issue rate.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the execute stage into an operand stage and an ALU/result stage. The operand stage resolves source values with the existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypass priorities and captures operands, immediate, and controls; the following stage performs the ALU operation and registers the result for MEM. Add a bypass from the immediately older ALU result into the operand-stage capture, and extend load-use interlocks so a consumer waits until a load value is available. Preserve single-instruction-per-cycle flow, dmem stall behavior, ID-resolved conditional branches, RVFI ordering, and correct squash/redirect handling across the added boundary. This separates the forwarding comparators/muxes from the wide ALU operation and should improve Fmax enough to offset the added control-transfer and load-use latency.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline payloads for captured forwarded operands, execution controls, and the added result-stage state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"\n…[61933 of 65005 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:02a4bc39eef72139]…\nmhz\": 54.423, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4449669, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3065, \"ff\": 583, \"seeds\": [52.581, 54.423, 54.423], \"perturbations\": [[0, 52.581, 19], [1, 54.423, 21], [2, 54.423, 21]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_7_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -14.018, \"arrival_ns\": 24.312, \"logic_cells\": 39, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_rf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 19, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T17:45:35.842356Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-001-r11s0 (improvement, +7.85%): Registering priority forwarding selects with the ID/EX consumer removes late destination-tag comparisons from the EX forwarding-to-ALU/address path; compute selects for producers' next pipeline positions and hold them with the consumer through stalls, while the load-use interlock handles loads.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
