{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Direct JAL call prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Conditional branches now resolve in ID, so predicting them adds fetch logic without avoiding the prior EX redirect cost. Direct JAL calls still wait for EX and flush younger work; CoreMark's repeated function calls make these jumps the remaining high-value prediction target.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Conditional branches now resolve in ID, so predicting them adds fetch logic without avoiding the prior EX redirect cost. Direct JAL calls still wait for EX and flush younger work; CoreMark's repeated function calls make these jumps the remaining high-value prediction target.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predict only aligned direct JAL instructions in fetch. Form their PC-relative target from the fetched J-immediate, redirect the fetch PC to that target, and carry a single predicted-JAL bit with the instruction. In EX, suppress the jump redirect only for a valid aligned JAL that was predicted; retain existing redirect and trap behavior for JALR and misaligned targets. Specializing prediction to direct JAL removes conditional-branch prediction logic and target metadata while avoiding the call redirect bubble on a correct prediction.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add one predicted-JAL bit to the fetch/decode and decode/execute pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize aligned JAL encodings, form their direct target in fetch, and select that target as the next PC while preserving bus-stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture the predicted-JAL bit with the instruction so EX ca