{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r10s0.yaml && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Share RV32M product hardware\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The latest measured critical path runs from EX forwarding through the ALU and back into the EX/MEM register. The ALU currently describes separate signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned 64-bit multipliers, so the M-extension datapath has parallel product cones and a wide result selection network.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute one unsigned 32-by-32 product and use it for MUL and MULHU. For MULHSU and MULH, correct the product's upper half by subtracting the unsigned operand corresponding to each signed negative input; leave the ALTOPS stand-ins unchanged. Sharing the main product should reduce multiplier and result-selection resources, ease placement around the EX datapath, and improve the forwarding-to-EX timing path without changing latency or architectural results.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Use one unsigned 64-bit product for all MUL variants and apply signed high-half corrections for MULH and MULHSU while preserving ALTOPS behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
