{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r14s0.yaml && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Reuse complementary branch comparisons\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The best core's timing path ends at the fetch PC and passes through the ID branch decision. The branch condition currently expresses both less-than and greater-or-equal separately for signed and unsigned comparisons, which can create redundant wide comparator logic on this redirect path.\nhypothesis: |\n  In ID, compute equality, signed less-than, and unsigned less-than once from the existing forwarded operands. Select BEQ/BNE from equality and its inverse, and BLT/BGE or BLTU/BGEU from the corresponding less-than result and its inverse. This keeps both signedness comparators and their inputs unchanged, avoids the operand transforms that hurt earlier shared-comparator attempts, and may reduce comparator duplication and the logic feeding the branch redirect without adding state or latency.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Share each signed or unsigned less-than comparison with its complementary BGE/BGEU condition, while retaining the direct equality path and forwarded operands.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
