mem address output. That address currently uses the general ALU result, whose final operation selection also includes the long M-extension arithmetic cones.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Expose the ALU's a+b result as a dedicated shared output and carry it to MEM as the effective address. Use it for dmem address generation and alignment checks, while retaining the general ALU result for writeback and RVFI. Load/store addresses are always rs1+immediate, so this bypasses the general operation result mux on the measured address path without adding a second adder.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a shared a+b result alongside the general ALU output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the dedicated effective address in the EX/MEM bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Register the dedicated add result as the memory effective address.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive dmem address and memory alignment checks from the dedicated address field.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a shared a+b result alongside the general ALU output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the dedicated effective address in the EX/MEM bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Register the dedicated add result as the memory effective address.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive dmem address and memory alignment checks from the dedicated address field.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 12.55, \"delta_pct\": 3.55, \"vs_baseline\": 3.55, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.639, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12324, \"ff\": 492, \"seeds\": [5.369, 5.639, 5.639], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.369, 153