{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r2s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-001-r2s0\ntitle: \"Predecode divider busy control\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current worst path runs from the ID/EX state through EX divider-op detection, fetch and hazard control, then back to the ID/EX stall input. Divider detection compares the ALU opcode against four encodings after the pipeline register, adding logic to this stall feedback path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Decode a single is_div control bit for validated DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU instructions and register it with the existing ID/EX control bundle. Use that bit in EX to identify divider instructions instead of comparing the ALU opcode against four constants. This moves the classification work before the ID/EX register and shortens the combinational path that asserts the multi-cycle stall, while preserving divider timing and arithmetic behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add an is_div bit to the pipelined control bundle.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Assert is_div only for validated M-extension divide and remainder instructions.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture the decoded is_div bit into ID/EX control state.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered is_div bit to drive divider instruction detection and busy control.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
