{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260930-002-r5s1\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260930-003-r7s2\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260930-002-r6s1\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "15:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Resolve conditional branches in decode\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Timing history identifies a control feedback path that passes through EX branch resolution, fetch redirection, hazard control, and decode. Conditional branches also keep younger instructions in flight until EX decides their direction. Moving only the conditional branch decision to decode should shorten that feedback path and reduce redirect bubbles without adding a pipeline stage.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Timing history identifies a control feedback path that passes through EX branch resolution, fetch redirection, hazard control, and decode. Conditional branches also keep younger instructions in flight until EX decides their direction. Moving only the conditional branch decision to decode should shorten that feedback path and reduce redirect bubbles without adding a pipeline stage.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Compute conditional branch comparisons and PC-relative targets in ID, then carry the resolved taken bit, target, and alignment result with the instruction into EX/MEM for RVFI reporting. Add EX/MEM and MEM/WB operand bypasses for ID branch comparisons, and hold fetch while a matching older writer is still in ID/EX or an older load has not reached MEM/WB. Redirect fetch as soon as an aligned branch is resolved in ID while still allowing that branch itself to enter ID/EX; keep JAL and JALR resolution in EX. Registering the branch outcome before EX removes the register-file-to-EX-to-fetch control chain and should improve Fmax while saving a cycle on taken branches.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the decode-resolved branch outcome, target, and misalignment state with the instruction through the pipeline for redirect and RVFI use.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve valid conditional branch comparisons and targets in decode using bypassed EX/MEM and MEM/WB operands.\"}\n…[9827 of 12899 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:446fc89987cde4e9]…\nession\", \"fitness\": 113.08, \"delta_pct\": -0.29, \"vs_baseline\": 833.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 50.167, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4436243, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3123, \"ff\": 590, \"seeds\": [49.266, 50.167, 50.167], \"perturbations\": [[0, 49.266, 16], [1, 50.167, 21], [2, 50.167, 21]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_1_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -15.298, \"arrival_ns\": 25.592, \"logic_cells\": 18, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T15:46:37.347539Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r7s2 (regression, -0.29%): Moving canonical `JALR` return redirects into ID still regressed slightly because return decoding, target selection, and alignment checks add work to the ID redirect path, while the EX bubbles saved were too few to offset that cost.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
