ddress once into a one-hot select and form the register-file read value with parallel masked-word reduction, retaining x0 behavior and the same-cycle write-first bypass. This may map the wide asynchronous reads into shallower FPGA LUT logic than the inferred binary-index mux trees, shortening the measured register-file-to-ID/EX path without adding pipeline state or changing stalls and forwarding. Keep the implementation limited to the read network so synthesis can compare the alternate mux topology directly. \nhyp-20260930-001-r4s0 | Direct effective address adder | regression 104.36 0.16 | cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s -> \n…[2038 of 5110 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:797c06cb85e3401e]…\ny-select structure. Compute the low byte and its carry, compute both carry-in versions of each upper byte in parallel, and select each byte sum and outgoing carry using the preceding block's carry. This keeps the architectural result and cycle timing unchanged while limiting serial carry propagation to byte-sized additions and carry-select muxes, which should improve the forwarding-to-effective-address path and reduce Fmax pressure on other ADD users. \nhyp-20260930-001-r8s0 | Bypass ALU result selection for memory addresses | regression 113.66 0.22 | cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0 -> dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\n   Expose the ALU's existing a+b result as a dedicated output and route that sum directly into the EX/MEM result field for loads and stores. Keep the general ALU output for all other instructions. Synthesis can share the existing adder, so this removes operation-result selection from the forwarding-to-address path without adding another adder, changing pipeline timing, or changing the effective-address calculation. \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
