esults.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add EX divide-busy stalling so younger instructions remain held until the divide result can advance, without repeatedly retiring older stages.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the EX divide-busy handshake to fetch/decode hazard control and preserve the existing\n…[33647 of 36719 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:39760c202007ca97]…\nta_pct\": -28.3, \"vs_baseline\": 570.96, \"fmax_mhz\": 36.96, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4545142, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3724, \"ff\": 663, \"seeds\": [35.958, 36.96, 36.96], \"perturbations\": [[0, 35.958, 23], [1, 36.96, 23], [2, 36.96, 23]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_addr_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_29_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -22.81, \"arrival_ns\": 33.104, \"logic_cells\": 25, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu\", \"cpu/u_mem\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 23, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T16:27:20.587491Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r9s1 (regression, -28.30%): A one-entry `mem_wb_t` skid with completion muxing and `pipeline_block`/redirect control regressed despite dmem stalls, showing that hiding at most one younger ALU instruction per request must justify the added register and control cost on CoreMark.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
