{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r14s1.yaml && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-002-r14s1\ntitle: \"Retiming older operand forwarding into decode\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The latest measured critical path runs from the writeback data mux through EX operand forwarding and the ALU to a memory-side output. An operand from the older EX/MEM instruction is already available while its consumer is in ID, so carrying that value into ID/EX can remove the MEM/WB-to-EX bypass mux from the execute datapath without adding a pipeline stage.\nhypothesis: |\n  Resolve the older EX/MEM producer match in ID and capture its final writeback value as the consumer's ID/EX source operand. Expose the current MEM-stage value, including load extraction, for that early bypass; the existing dmem stall must hold ID/EX until a load response is ready. Keep the ID/EX-to-EX/MEM forwarding for the immediately preceding producer, retain register-file write-through for values already in WB, and remove the older MEM/WB forwarding selection from EX. This retimes the common two-cycle dependency path across an existing register boundary while preserving instruction throughput, branch timing, and load-use behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Route the resolved current MEM-stage writeback value to ID so older EX/MEM dependencies can be captured before EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the current instruction's final writeback value, including aligned and extended load data, for ID-stage bypass.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture matching EX/MEM producer values into ID/EX operands and retain forwarding selection only for an ID/EX producer.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Remove the MEM/WB forwarding choice from EX operand muxes while preserving the immediately older EX/MEM bypass.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
