{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r15s1.yaml; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-002-r15s1\ntitle: \"Register the fetch to decode boundary\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The recent critical path runs through fetch, the register file, ID branch\n  resolution, and back into the fetch PC control. This couples instruction\n  arrival and bus readiness to branch resolution in one combinational loop.\n  Breaking that loop can raise Fmax, which is currently the largest lever on\n  CoreMark fitness.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add an IF/ID instruction register with PC and valid state, keeping the\n  register file's asynchronous reads. Let fetch fill or hold this slot under\n  imem backpressure, and have ID consume its registered instruction while\n  resolving conditional branches and issuing redirects. Flush the slot on\n  redirects and preserve load-use, divider, and data-stall hold behavior.\n  The new stage boundary removes the current combinational fetch-to-register-\n  file-to-ID-to-fetch feedback path; steady-state instruction flow remains\n  one per cycle, while the extra branch recovery latency is expected to be\n  limited on CoreMark.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define the registered fetch/decode payload including instruction, PC, and validity.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add an IF/ID register with correct fetch acceptance, backpressure hold, and redirect flush behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume the registered instruction while retaining asynchronous register-file reads and ID branch resolution.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the new front-end stage and update stall and flush control for the additional pipeline boundary.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Adjust hazard control so the fetch slot, ID/EX stage, and redirect flushes remain coordinated.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
