{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r3s1.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260930-002-r3s1\ntitle: \\\"Register the branch redirect boundary\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The measured critical path crosses the EX branch decision, fetch PC selection, hazard control, and back into ID. That same-cycle redirect feedback couples datapath depth across several pipeline stages and currently limits Fmax. The earlier predictor attempts also show that adding more fetch-time decision logic is costly.\nhypothesis: |\n  Put a register boundary between EX branch/jump resolution and fetch redirection. EX will capture a valid redirect and its target when the instruction can advance; IF will apply the pending target on the following cycle. During that cycle, registered pending state will squash the wrong-path ID/EX instruction before it can enter EX/MEM and flush the younger fetched instruction, while suppressing any redirect from the squashed instruction. This adds a control-transfer bubble, but removes the EX-to-IF-to-hazard-to-ID combinational feedback path and should raise Fmax enough to offset the small CoreMark IPC cost. Preserve redirect priority over instruction-fetch stalls, defer capture while a data-memory stall holds EX, and retain the existing misalignment trap behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Add a pending redirect/target register and connect the delayed redirect handshake to fetch, hazard control, and EX squash logic.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Expose branch/jump redirect resolution for capture, and suppress execution or redirect from the younger instruction during a pending squash cycle.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \\\"Use registered redirect-pending state for fetch/decode flushing so EX resolution no longer drives the hazard feedback path combinationally.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Apply the registered redirect target with priority over stalls and suppress the sequential wrong-path fetch while the redirect is pending.\\\"\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
