{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r4s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r4s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Synchronous register-file read stage\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's measured critical path runs from register-file state through the operand read and pipeline control logic into ID/EX. The previous asynchronous register-file rewrite failed to infer LUT RAM and added validity gating to the read path. A pipeline change that supports synchronous memory reads can remove the wide asynchronous selection network from the cycle path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add an explicit IF/ID instruction register and make the two register-file reads synchronous, aligning the returned operands with the decoded instruction as it enters EX. Preserve one-instruction-per-cycle flow with registered decode metadata and the existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding, and hold or flush the new front-end stage under load-use, divider, memory, and redirect conditions. Removing asynchronous 32-entry read selection from the register-file-to-ID/EX path should enable FPGA memory inference and raise Fmax; the deeper front end costs pipeline fill and some control-transfer latency but does not reduce steady-state issue rate.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: \"Implement registered dual-read behavior suitable for FPGA memory inference, with x0 and write-first forwarding semantics preserved.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend pipeline bundles for the registered IF/ID instruction and aligned decoded control and operand metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add an IF/ID instruction register with correct hold, redirect, flush, and fetch-stall behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Align synchronous register-file outputs with the decoded instruction entering EX and preserve hazard and flush behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the registered fetch/decode and register-file read stages while retaining the existing retirement and bus contracts.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
