{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r7s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-002-r7s1\ntitle: \"Split operand forwarding from execute\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current best's measured critical path starts at MEM/WB forwarding state and runs through the EX forwarding network and ALU toward the data-memory address output. These are two wide selection and arithmetic operations in one timing stage. A structural pipeline boundary between operand selection and execution can let each settle in its own cycle without lowering steady-state issue rate.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the execute stage into an operand stage and an ALU/result stage. The operand stage resolves source values with the existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypass priorities and captures operands, immediate, and controls; the following stage performs the ALU operation and registers the result for MEM. Add a bypass from the immediately older ALU result into the operand-stage capture, and extend load-use interlocks so a consumer waits until a load value is available. Preserve single-instruction-per-cycle flow, dmem stall behavior, ID-resolved conditional branches, RVFI ordering, and correct squash/redirect handling across the added boundary. This separates the forwarding comparators/muxes from the wide ALU operation and should improve Fmax enough to offset the added control-transfer and load-use latency.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add pipeline payloads for captured forwarded operands, execution controls, and the added result-stage state.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Divide operand forwarding and ALU/result generation across the new execution stages, including the adjacent-result bypass and divider handshake.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Extend load-use, redirect, divide, and memory-stall control to hold or squash the correct instructions across the added execution boundary.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Wire the split execution pipeline while preserving the existing bus and single-channel RVFI contracts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
