{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r8s1.yaml && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Generate memory addresses in decode\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The best design's measured critical path runs from a forwarded register value through the EX operand mux and ALU to the data-memory address. The prior EX/MEM carry-select split shortened that path by only 3.32% and added partial-sum registers and a MEM mux. Moving the memory address calculation to the existing decode stage removes forwarding and the full-width addition from the memory-request path altogether.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute load and store effective addresses in ID from the decoded immediate and the existing register-file/bypass values, then carry the address through ID/EX and EX/MEM for the MEM request, alignment checks, and RVFI memory metadata. Add ID interlocks for a matching writer still in ID/EX and for a matching load in EX/MEM, so the address uses the current value from the existing EX/MEM or MEM/WB bypass. This structurally separates memory address generation from EX forwarding and arithmetic without adding a pipeline stage; the added dependency bubbles apply only when a memory base is not yet available.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add an effective-address field to the ID/EX and EX/MEM pipeline bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Calculate effective addresses for valid loads and stores using the decoded immediate and bypassed rs1 value.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Interlock ID memory operations behind a matching ID/EX writer or an EX/MEM load so address calculation sees the correct base.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect memory-operation classification and base-register dependency information to the hazard control.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Carry the decode-generated effective address through EX/MEM alongside the normal ALU result.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the carried effective address for dmem requests, alignment checks, and aligned RVFI memory addresses.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
