{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; p=Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r9s1.yaml\\\"); print(p.resolve()); print(p.read_text())'\"","aggregated_output":"/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep4/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260930-002-r9s1-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r9s1.yaml\nid: hyp-20260930-002-r9s1\ntitle: \"Overlap data stalls with one younger instruction\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current memory backpressure policy freezes the whole pipeline whenever an EX/MEM load or store sees io_dmemReady low. Those cycles prevent even independent ALU work from advancing, although the single-issue pipeline can safely compute a younger instruction while the older memory request waits.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry in-order completion skid buffer around the MEM/WB boundary. When a data request stalls, retain its request and architectural record, allow one younger independent non-memory instruction to execute into the buffer, and then stop issuing until the request completes. Keep retirement in program order: retire the memory operation only when its bus handshake completes, then retire the buffered instruction. Preserve load-use interlocks for any younger instruction that reads the outstanding load destination, and keep memory requests ordered. This overlaps short dmem stalls with useful execution without widening retirement or changing the RVFI contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define the compact state needed to retain a stalled memory instruction and one younger completion.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the pending-memory and buffered-completion state while retaining the single-channel retirement interface.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Hold a memory request stable until ready and capture load data on its completing handshake.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Allow one independent younger instruction to advance during a data stall, then block issue and preserve load dependency interlocks.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Route the one admitted younger result into the completion buffer without replaying the pending memory operation.\"\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
