{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r10s2.yaml && rg -n '\\\"required\\\"|\\\"category\\\"|\\\"file\\\"|fitness_delta_pct|confidence' cores/bench/schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-003-r10s2\ntitle: \"Compact return-target prediction\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The best measured predictor so far was a one-entry cache for canonical JALR returns, but its full-width PC tag, target, and carried prediction target kept the gain below the acceptance threshold. Return addresses are aligned and CoreMark code occupies a small address region, so a compact partial-tag and low-target representation can reduce lookup and pipeline state costs while retaining EX correction for aliases.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep a single-entry return-target cache trained by valid, aligned canonical JALR returns in EX, but store only the return-PC bits [15:2] as its tag and target bits [19:2]. In IF, recognize canonical returns and compare the partial tag; on a hit, reconstruct the predicted target from the current PC's [31:20] and the cached target bits, then fetch from it. Carry only prediction-valid plus the 18 predicted target bits through ID/EX. In EX, compare the resolved full target against the reconstructed prediction and redirect on any tag alias, target mismatch, or predicted return that resolves as misaligned; the latter must resume at pc+4 while preserving the existing trap. This reduces tag compare width and predictor/pipeline storage while keeping prediction advisory and precise correction behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry a return-prediction-valid bit and the 18 aligned low target bits instead of a full 32-bit predicted PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use a single cache entry with a 14-bit aligned partial PC tag and 18-bit aligned target; reconstruct the fetch target from the current PC's upper bits.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture the compact return prediction metadata with the decoded instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the actual full return target with the carried prediction and correct aliases, target mismatches, and misaligned-return predictions.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect EX return training and resolved-target signals to the compact IF predictor.\"\nrg: cores/bench/schemas/hypothesis.schema.json: IO error for operation on cores/bench/schemas/hypothesis.schema.json: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
