{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": ?\\\"predictor\\\"|predictor|branch predictor|direction table' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Early backward-taken branch prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently redirects only after branch resolution in EX, flushing younger work and losing cycles on every taken branch and direct jump. CoreMark repeatedly executes backward loop branches, so predicting their target in fetch can avoid those recurring redirect bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently redirects only after branch resolution in EX, flushing younger work and losing cycles on every taken branch and direct jump. CoreMark repeatedly executes backward loop branches, so predicting their target in fetch can avoid those recurring redirect bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a static branch predictor that predicts valid backward conditional branches taken and forward conditional branches not taken, and predicts direct JAL instructions taken. Compute the predicted next PC in fetch, carry it with the instruction through decode, and redirect from EX only when the resolved next PC differs from the prediction. Gate prediction on an available instruction and fall back to sequential fetch for misaligned targets. Correct predictions should remove the current two younger-instruction flush penalty on common loop branches and direct jumps without adding predictor state.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the fetch/decode and decode/execute pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predict backward conditional branches taken, forward branches not taken, and direct JAL targets in fetch; select the predicted PC while preserving stall and alignment behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the fetch prediction metadata into the ID/EX register with the decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved next PC with the carried prediction and \n…[59325 of 62397 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:66c96c012a41c808]…\ne\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 125.78, \"delta_pct\": 2.84, \"vs_baseline\": 937.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 56.856, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4520226, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3193, \"ff\": 656, \"seeds\": [58.134, 56.856, 56.856], \"perturbations\": [[0, 58.134, 11], [1, 56.856, 11], [2, 56.856, 11]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.mem_to_reg_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -12.202, \"arrival_ns\": 22.496, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_wb\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T18:26:50.617031Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r13s2 (regression, +2.84%): Doubling the direction table to 16 PC[5:2]-indexed counters still regressed CoreMark, so added capacity alone did not make fetch-time predictions accurate enough to repay EX-stage correction redirects on misses.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(p)]; [(print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"],r[\\\"outcome\\\"],r.get(\\\"delta_pct\\\"),r.get(\\\"fitness\\\"),r[\\\"expected_impact\\\"][\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\"],\\\"\\\\n\\\",r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"][:1100],\\\"\\\\n---\\\")) for r in rows if r.get(\\\"category\\\")==\\\"predictor\\\"]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(p)]; [(print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"],r[\\\"outcome\\\"],r.get(\\\"delta_pct\\\"),r.get(\\\"fitness\\\"),r[\\\"expected_impact\\\"][\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\"],\\\"\\\\n\\\",r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"][:1100],\\\"\\\\n---\\\")) for r in rows if r.get(\\\"category\\\")==\\\"predictor\\\"]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260930-003-r1s2 Early backward-taken branch prediction regression 3.3 12.52 5 \n Add a static branch predictor that predicts valid backward conditional branches taken and forward conditional branches not taken, and predicts direct JAL instructions taken. Compute the predicted next PC in fetch, carry it with the instruction through decode, and redirect from EX only when the resolved next PC differs from the prediction. Gate prediction on an available instruction and fall back to sequential fetch for misaligned targets. Correct predictions should remove the current two younger-instruction flush penalty on common loop branches and direct jumps without adding predictor state.\n \n---\nhyp-20260930-003-r2s2 EX-trained return address stack prediction regression -2.79 101.28 6 \n Add a small return address stack (RAS) whose entries are pushed in EX for valid JAL/JALR calls writing x1 or x5, and popped for valid JALR returns reading x1 or x5 into x0. In fetch, recognize the standard return encoding and use the RAS top as its predicted next PC when the stack is nonempty. Carry the predicted next PC with the instruction and make EX redirect only when its resolved next PC differs. Updating the RAS only as calls and returns advance through EX avoids speculative stack changes; the small registered target lookup should predict common ABI returns without adding branch-immediate decoding and addition to the fetch path.\n \n---\nhyp-20260930-003-r3s2 Four-entry tagged branch target buffer regression -20.37 82.97 6 \n Add a four-entry fully associative branch target buffer with full-PC tags, stored targets, a conditional-transfer bit, and two-bit saturating direction counters. Fetch compares the current PC against the four tags in parallel; on a hit, it predicts a conditional branch according to its counter and predicts learned JAL/JALR targets taken. Train entries only when valid branch or jump instructions advance from EX, retaining the branch target even on not-taken outcomes and excluding misaligned transfers. Carry the predicted\n…[6796 of 9868 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d2b058cd48b00f41]…\ne deferred branches in EX from the forwarded operands and correct fetch to the branch target or sequential PC on a wrong prediction, preserving misalignment traps and existing stall/flush priority. This should recover branch-hazard cycles on common loop iterations without adding a predictor table or putting immediate target generation on the fetch path.\n \n---\nhyp-20260930-003-r13s2 Reduce branch predictor aliasing regression 2.84 125.78 5 \n Replace the eight-entry direction table with a 16-entry, two-bit saturating-counter table indexed by instruction PC bits [5:2]. Predict conditional direction in fetch, carry the prediction with the instruction, and retain EX-stage correction only for a direction miss. Train from resolved legal conditional branches in ID. The extra eight counters should reduce destructive aliasing at modest storage cost, improving prediction accuracy enough to offset the occasional miss-recovery bubble while preserving the branch target and stall handling used by the existing design.\n \n---\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
