{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\":\\\"predictor\\\"|category: predictor|branch predictor|direction table|return cache|BTB|RAS' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Early backward-taken branch prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently redirects only after branch resolution in EX, flushing younger work and losing cycles on every taken branch and direct jump. CoreMark repeatedly executes backward loop branches, so predicting their target in fetch can avoid those recurring redirect bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently redirects only after branch resolution in EX, flushing younger work and losing cycles on every taken branch and direct jump. CoreMark repeatedly executes backward loop branches, so predicting their target in fetch can avoid those recurring redirect bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a static branch predictor that predicts valid backward conditional branches taken and forward conditional branches not taken, and predicts direct JAL instructions taken. Compute the predicted next PC in fetch, carry it with the instruction through decode, and redirect from EX only when the resolved next PC differs from the prediction. Gate prediction on an available instruction and fall back to sequential fetch for misaligned targets. Correct predictions should remove the current two younger-instruction flush penalty on common loop branches and direct jumps without adding predictor state.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the fetch/decode and decode/execute pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predict backward conditional branches taken, forward branches not taken, and direct JAL targets in fetch; select the predicted PC while preserving stall and alignment behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the fetch prediction metadata into the ID/EX register with the decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved next PC with the carried prediction and \n…[36182 of 39254 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:14cb4cc2fb4671de]…\ntion\": \"Correct the fetch PC only when the resolved branch direction disagrees with its carried prediction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect table training and misprediction recovery signals through the pipeline.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 112.34, \"delta_pct\": -8.15, \"vs_baseline\": 826.9, \"fmax_mhz\": 50.621, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4506098, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3335, \"ff\": 682, \"seeds\": [54.289, 50.621, 50.621], \"perturbations\": [[0, 54.289, 20], [1, 50.621, 20], [2, 50.621, 20]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_3_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/direction_table_direction_table_RAMREG_1_G[22]_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -13.42, \"arrival_ns\": 23.714, \"logic_cells\": 46, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_rf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 20, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T18:49:20.146641Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r15s2.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260930-003-r15s2\ntitle: \\\"Predict only dependency-stalled branches\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Branches whose operands are already available resolve in ID with no redirect penalty, so broad fetch prediction adds lookup and recovery cost to paths that do not need it. The remaining avoidable control-flow delay is the branch dependency interlock while a recent producer reaches a usable forwarding stage.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a compact PC-indexed two-bit direction table that is consulted only when an ID-stage branch has an unresolved EX or load dependency. Let these branches advance using the predicted direction, while retaining the existing exact ID comparison and redirect path for branches with available operands. Carry a speculative-branch marker and prediction through ID/EX; in EX, compare the actual forwarded operands for marked branches, train their counters, and redirect only on a miss. Train nondependent branches from their existing ID-resolved outcome. This targets branch-stall cycles while avoiding predictor lookup, target selection, and recovery logic on the common independent-branch path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \\\"Carry the prediction and speculative-branch marker with ID/EX branch metadata.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \\\"Expose branch dependency conditions so ID can bypass the interlock only for a predicted branch.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Add a small direction table and use it only for branches whose operands are not yet available; retain exact ID resolution otherwise.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Resolve marked branches from forwarded EX operands, train the predictor, and correct the PC only on a direction miss.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Connect dependency prediction, counter training, and EX misprediction recovery without changing the RVFI contract.\\\"\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r15s2.yaml')\nprint(p.exists(), p.stat().st_size)\nprint(p.read_text())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
