{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses && cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r1s2.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260930-003-r1s2\ntitle: \\\"Early backward-taken branch prediction\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The five-stage pipeline currently redirects only after branch resolution in EX, flushing younger work and losing cycles on every taken branch and direct jump. CoreMark repeatedly executes backward loop branches, so predicting their target in fetch can avoid those recurring redirect bubbles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a static branch predictor that predicts valid backward conditional branches taken and forward conditional branches not taken, and predicts direct JAL instructions taken. Compute the predicted next PC in fetch, carry it with the instruction through decode, and redirect from EX only when the resolved next PC differs from the prediction. Gate prediction on an available instruction and fall back to sequential fetch for misaligned targets. Correct predictions should remove the current two younger-instruction flush penalty on common loop branches and direct jumps without adding predictor state.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \\\"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the fetch/decode and decode/execute pipeline bundles.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Predict backward conditional branches taken, forward branches not taken, and direct JAL targets in fetch; select the predicted PC while preserving stall and alignment behavior.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Carry the fetch prediction metadata into the ID/EX register with the decoded instruction.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Compare the resolved next PC with the carried prediction and request a redirect only on a misprediction.\\\"\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
