{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The only logged predictor attempt used static backward-taken/JAL prediction and missed the acceptance threshold. I’m proposing a small return address stack instead: it targets function returns without putting branch-offset target addition on the fetch path."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses && cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r2s2.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260930-003-r2s2\ntitle: \\\"EX-trained return address stack prediction\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The five-stage core resolves JALR returns in EX, so every function return redirects fetch and flushes younger instructions. CoreMark makes repeated calls and returns, and return targets are predictable from the call stack even when an indirect target cannot be inferred from the instruction bits.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small return address stack (RAS) whose entries are pushed in EX for valid JAL/JALR calls writing x1 or x5, and popped for valid JALR returns reading x1 or x5 into x0. In fetch, recognize the standard return encoding and use the RAS top as its predicted next PC when the stack is nonempty. Carry the predicted next PC with the instruction and make EX redirect only when its resolved next PC differs. Updating the RAS only as calls and returns advance through EX avoids speculative stack changes; the small registered target lookup should predict common ABI returns without adding branch-immediate decoding and addition to the fetch path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the fetch/decode and decode/execute bundles.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Recognize JALR returns, select the nonempty RAS top as the predicted PC, and accept EX-stage push/pop updates while respecting instruction stalls and flushes.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Carry predicted-next-PC metadata into the ID/EX register with its instruction.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Compare the resolved next PC with the carried prediction and suppress redirects for correctly predicted returns.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect EX call/return classification and update controls to the fetch-stage RAS.\nEOF\ncat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r2s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
