{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses && cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r4s2.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260930-003-r4s2\ntitle: \\\"Compact static direct-transfer predictor\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior fetch predictors reduced redirect bubbles but lost fitness to fetch lookup cost, target storage, or 32-bit predicted-PC metadata. The core currently resolves branches and direct jumps in EX, so correctly predicting common backward loops and JALs can still save recurring redirects if the predictor carries much less state.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict valid backward conditional branches taken, forward branches not taken, and aligned direct JAL targets taken in IF. Compute branch and JAL targets from the instruction already being fetched, and carry only one predicted-taken bit through ID/EX rather than a 32-bit predicted next PC. In EX, redirect only when the resolved transfer direction differs from that bit; direct predicted targets are derived from the same PC and immediate. Do not predict reserved branch encodings or misaligned targets. This retains the low-state BTFN/JAL policy while reducing pipeline metadata and EX comparison logic relative to earlier predictor versions.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add a single predicted-taken bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles, without carrying a predicted PC.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Decode valid branch and JAL instructions for static direction prediction, compute aligned direct targets, and select the predicted fetch PC.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Capture the predicted-taken bit alongside the decoded instruction.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Compare the resolved transfer direction with the carried bit and redirect only for mispredictions, preserving misalignment traps and JALR behavior.\nEOF\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
