{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r5s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-003-r5s2\ntitle: \"Shallow explicit-register return stack predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Calls and returns in CoreMark repeatedly redirect the five-stage pipeline, but earlier predictors lost fitness to fetch-time target arithmetic, associative tag checks, or a variable-indexed return stack. ABI return targets can be learned from calls without computing branch targets in fetch.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the indexed eight-entry RAS approach with a two-entry return stack implemented as explicit top and next-target registers plus a small depth state. Push PC+4 when a valid call advances from EX and pop on a valid return; fetch recognizes only canonical JALR returns and predicts the registered top target when the stack is nonempty. Carry a return-prediction flag and target with that instruction, then let EX suppress its redirect only when the actual resolved next PC matches the carried target. This keeps fetch lookup to return decode and a direct register read, with no branch-immediate target adder or variable-indexed stack mux, while covering shallow call nesting common in CoreMark.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add return-prediction validity and target metadata to the fetch/decode and ID/EX bundles.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Recognize canonical JALR returns and select the explicit RAS top register when nonempty; accept qualified push/pop updates.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Carry return-prediction metadata with its instruction into ID/EX.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Expose advancing call/return updates and suppress redirects only for matching predicted return targets.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect EX-qualified call/return updates to the fetch-stage two-entry return stack.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
